From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:05:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: clear USB role when partner lacks USB data

Adopted from ROCKNIX (SM8750 0509, f0703a06).

0c8ee850572 gated the "no USB data -> USB_ROLE_NONE" decision behind
UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB. Without that quirk the role is never cleared for a
charger-only partner, so it stays attached across suspend, and unplugging
while suspended can hang the SoC. Clear the role whenever the partner
advertises no USB data.

Signed-off-by: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
index c1450639c7956517ad3f313e1e494b2b0f6c52a0..aee0377594c33fd56f5d6e47af0517858077acc8 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -1367,10 +1367,8 @@ static void ucsi_partner_change(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 			typec_partner_set_usb_mode(con->partner, USB_MODE_USB4);
 	}
 
-	if ((!UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB)) &&
-	    ((con->ucsi->quirks & UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB) &&
-	     (!(UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN3) ||
-		UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN4)))))
+	/* Only notify USB controller if partner supports USB data */
+	if (!(UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB)))
 		u_role = USB_ROLE_NONE;
 
 	ret = usb_role_switch_set_role(con->usb_role_sw, u_role);
